{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS42uYRxS2tPkXyK1Vi7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish fails because `similarity()` returns a Python float and boto3 refuses to store floats. I fixed it in `src/app.py`, and the cause and fix are written up in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Why only the second publish:** the first one runs against an empty table, so `similar` is an empty list and no score gets written. From the second publish on, `similar` holds float scores. `put_item` then raises `TypeError: Float types are not supported`, which `logs/error.log` shows and the handler turns into a 500.\n\n**The fix:**\n- **Conversion:** a new `to_dynamo()` converts floats to `Decimal`, going through `str` so the stored value is exact. `publish()` runs the item through it right before `put_item`. Any float added to the item later is converted too, not just `score`.\n- **Tests:** I added two tests that publish a second story into a populated table, one through `publish()` and one through `handler()` expecting a 201. All three tests pass with the fix, and with `src/` stashed the new tests fail.\n\n**Colleague's note:** I used its diagnosis, the idea of converting at the write boundary, and the advice to seed the table before testing a write. I did not use integer percentages, because `Decimal` keeps the stored scores as they are. I also did not publish twice against a real table, since I'm not touching anything outside this directory. The fake table rejects floats the same way boto3 does. `ANSWER.md` lists which parts applied and which didn't.\n\nI haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":752,"cache_read_input_tokens":26146,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":752},"output_tokens":489,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"s